{"result":"{
  "metadata": {
    "id": "458948614",
    "title": "TSD-SFCC-708 — PDP Related Colours: Cross-Linked Swatch Navigation",
    "type": "page",
    "created": "",
    "updated": "",
    "url": "https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/SFCC/pages/458948614",
    "space": {
      "key": "SFCC",
      "name": "Adobe SFCC"
    },
    "version": 3,
    "attachments": [],
    "content": {
      "value": "| **Field** | **Value** |\n| --- | --- |\n| **Document ID** | TSD-SFCC-708 |\n| **Author(s)** | Victor T. Crisostomo — Squad A / Technical Architect |\n| **Reviewer(s)** | [Technical Lead Name] — Technical Lead |\n| **Created** | 31 Aug 2026 |\n| **Version** | v0.3 — Draft |\n| **Status** | Draft |\n| **Related Jira** | SFCC-708 |\n\n---\n\nVersion History\n---------------\n\n| Version | Date | Summary of Change | Author |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| v0.1 | 31 Aug 2026 | Initial draft | Victor T. Crisostomo |\n| v0.2 | 31 Aug 2026 | Section 5 updated to match codebase: hook function is `modifyGETResponse` on existing `productModifyGETResponse.js`; no `hooks.json` change required; response field is a native array (no `JSON.stringify`); `colourValue` (Australian spelling); `product.online` used directly; iterator pattern with `hasNext()/next()`; `empty()` for null checks; `pdpURL` removed from swatch payload — PWA Kit constructs URL from `masterProductID` + `colourValue` | Victor T. Crisostomo |\n| v0.3 | 31 Aug 2026 | Section 6 added — PWA Kit frontend implementation plan | Victor T. Crisostomo |\n\n---\n\n1. Problem Statement\n--------------------\n\n### 1.1 Context\n\nZimmermann products are catalogued in SFCC as separate master products when they share a colourway family but carry distinct style codes (e.g. `9536JF261BLK` and `9536JF261CRM`). Because these are independent masters, they do not share a variation model and therefore cannot display each other's colour variants through the standard SFCC variation attribute mechanism. The previous platform (Magento) allowed merchandisers to manually link such products via a comma-separated style code field, giving shoppers a unified colour swatch row across related PDPs.\n\n### 1.2 Problem\n\nSFCC has no native mechanism to surface colour swatches from a different master product on the current PDP. As a result, shoppers browsing a product in one colour have no discoverable path to related colourways that are catalogued under separate master IDs — reducing colour discovery and cross-sell opportunity. There is also no Business Manager UI for merchandisers to declare these cross-product relationships.\n\n### 1.3 Impact if Not Solved\n\nShoppers who land on one colourway PDP cannot discover related colours, which replicates a known gap from the Magento platform and fails to meet the stated merchandising requirement. Conversion for colour-driven products (a core Zimmermann category) is negatively affected. The PWA Kit frontend team is blocked from building swatch UI components without a defined backend data contract.\n\n### 1.4 Success Criteria\n\n* A merchandiser can configure related master product IDs against any product in Business Manager using the `relatedMasterProductID` attribute (Set of Strings).\n* The SCAPI product response for a PDP includes a `c_relatedSwatches` array containing swatch data (colour value, display name, swatch image URL) for all online related master products.\n* Related colour swatches that belong to a product whose `online` flag is `false`, or whose current date falls outside the configured online start/end date range, are excluded from the response.\n* Clicking a cross-linked swatch navigates to the correct related master PDP, pre-selected on the right colour variant, with a full page load.\n* The solution works across all 7 storefronts (AU, UK, US Dom, US Intl, EU, ME) without per-market configuration.\n\n---\n\n2. Constraints & Assumptions\n----------------------------\n\n### 2.1 Constraints\n\n| Constraint | Detail |\n| --- | --- |\n| Platform | SFCC B2C Commerce + PWA Kit on MRT. No alternative platform in scope. |\n| Storefront layer | PWA Kit (React / SCAPI). No SFRA templates involved. Backend logic must be exposed via SCAPI hook — no direct ProductMgr access from the frontend. |\n| Storefront scope | Solution must work across all 7 storefronts. No single-market workarounds. |\n| Online filtering | Visibility of cross-linked swatches is controlled by the related product's `online` property (SFCC's computed `Product.online` accounts for the online flag and the `onlineFrom`/`onlineTo` date window — no manual date arithmetic required in the hook). This is an approved AC from ticket comments (Dani Rivett, 13 Aug 2026). |\n| Image gallery hover | Swatch interaction in the expanded image gallery (no full-page refresh) is OUT OF SCOPE for this TSD. The requirement is unresolved (see Section 8 — Risks). Swatch click on the main PDP results in a full-page navigation to the related PDP. |\n\n### 2.2 Assumptions\n\n| Assumption | Risk if Wrong |\n| --- | --- |\n| The `relatedMasterProductID` custom attribute (Set of Strings) is already configured in the SFCC product catalog XML and is available in Business Manager. | SCAPI hook cannot read the attribute; the entire data contract breaks. Catalog XML changes require a deployment. |\n| Swatch images are stored as variation attribute images on the `color` variation attribute (standard SFCC pattern). | Image URL construction in the hook will need to change; PWA Kit swatch image rendering logic will differ from existing swatches. |\n| The `color` variation attribute ID is consistent across all masters in scope. | Attribute lookup in the hook will fail silently for any master using a different attribute ID. |\n| The relationship is configured bidirectionally by merchandisers in BM (Master A references Master B, and Master B references Master A). | Only one PDP in a pair shows cross-linked swatches; the other is invisible to the shopper. No automatic mirroring is implemented at this stage. |\n| The PWA Kit frontend will consume the `c_relatedSwatches` extension field and handle rendering, navigation (constructing the PDP URL from `masterProductID` + `colourValue`), and any \"active swatch\" state management client-side. | If frontend expects a different payload shape, both sides need to change. Contract must be agreed before frontend development starts. |\n\n---\n\n3. Options Analysis\n-------------------\n\n### 3.1 Options Summary\n\n| Option | Pros | Cons | Viable? |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| **Option A** — Extend existing `dw.ocapi.shop.product.modifyGETResponse` hook in `productModifyGETResponse.js` | + Uses the already-registered hook and established pattern (same file as product badges TSD-SFCC-225); no new endpoint or new hook registration; server-side filtering keeps online logic off the frontend; cached at CDN with the product response | - Adds latency to every product GET if related products are fetched synchronously; ProductMgr lookups are synchronous; must be bounded to avoid slow PDPs | Yes — Recommended |\n| **Option B** — Custom SCAPI endpoint (`/related-swatches/{masterID}`) | + Lazy-loadable; no impact on base product GET latency; easier to cache independently | - Extra network round-trip from PWA Kit on every PDP load; more surface area to maintain and version; PWA Kit must handle loading state for swatches separately | Yes |\n| **Option C** — Client-side OCAPI/SCAPI call from PWA Kit | + No backend changes beyond catalog attribute | - Online/published filtering logic must live in the frontend — violates separation of concerns; exposes unpublished product IDs to the client; not consistent with existing data-fetching patterns in this codebase | No |\n\n### 3.2 Option Detail\n\n#### Option A — Extend `modifyGETResponse` hook (Recommended)\n\nThe existing `dw.ocapi.shop.product.modifyGETResponse` hook in `plugin_zim_scapi/cartridge/scripts/hooks/shop/productModifyGETResponse.js` already handles product badge enrichment (TSD-SFCC-225). The related swatches logic is added as a second enrichment block in the same exported `modifyGETResponse` function, in its own `try/catch` so a swatch failure cannot affect badge enrichment. The hook reads `relatedMasterProductID` from the current master product, iterates over each related product ID using `ProductMgr.getProduct()`, applies online filtering via SFCC's computed `product.online` property, and appends a `c_relatedSwatches` array to the response. No `hooks.json` change is required — the hook is already registered.\n\n#### Option B — Custom SCAPI endpoint\n\nA new custom SCAPI endpoint would accept a master product ID and return only the related swatch data. This option defers the network call to after initial PDP render, which avoids adding to the critical-path product GET. However, it introduces an additional loading state in the PWA Kit swatch component and creates a new endpoint to maintain. Given that the swatch row is expected to be visible on initial PDP render (per design), the lazy-load benefit does not outweigh the added complexity.\n\n#### Option C — Client-side call (Discarded)\n\nDiscarded — requires online/published filtering to be performed client-side, which would expose unpublished product IDs in the browser and is inconsistent with the project's existing data-fetching architecture.\n\n---\n\n4. Recommended Option & Rationale\n---------------------------------\n\n### 4.1 Recommended Option\n\n**Option A — Extend the existing `dw.ocapi.shop.product.modifyGETResponse` hook**\n\n### 4.2 Rationale\n\nOption A is recommended because the hook is already registered, the file is already in production handling badge enrichment, and the same pattern (iterating SFCC API results, enriching the response object with a native array, wrapping in `try/catch`) is proven. There is no additional round-trip, no new endpoint to maintain, and online filtering uses SFCC's own computed `product.online` — no custom date arithmetic. The same hook pattern was used for Product Badges (TSD-SFCC-225), so it is a known, tested pattern in this codebase.\n\n### 4.3 Trade-offs Accepted\n\nThe hook executes synchronous `ProductMgr.getProduct()` calls for each related product ID. If a product has many related masters (e.g. 5+), this adds measurable latency to the product GET. This is mitigated by bounding the maximum number of related IDs processed per request (`MAX_RELATED_SWATCHES = 5`) and by the expectation that most products will have 1–3 related masters. This trade-off is accepted over Option B's additional network round-trip.\n\n---\n\n5. SFCC Backend Implementation\n------------------------------\n\n### 5.1 High-Level Sequence\n\n1. Shopper navigates to a PDP; PWA Kit issues a SCAPI GET `/products/{masterID}`.\n2. SFCC assembles the standard product response.\n3. The `modifyGETResponse` hook fires; it resolves the master product (using `product.getMasterProduct()` if the product is a variant).\n4. The hook reads `masterProduct.custom.relatedMasterProductID` (Set of Strings).\n5. If the set is empty or null, the hook exits with no change to the response.\n6. For each related product ID in the set (up to `MAX_RELATED_SWATCHES = 5`), the hook calls `ProductMgr.getProduct(relatedID)`.\n7. If the product is null, not a master (`!relatedProduct.master`), or not online (`!relatedProduct.online`), it is skipped with an appropriate `Logger` entry.\n8. For each valid online related master, the hook reads the `color` variation attribute values from the product's variation model.\n9. For each colour value, the hook constructs: `masterProductID`, `colourValue`, `displayName`, `swatchImageURL`.\n10. The hook sets `response.c_relatedSwatches` as a native array on the response object.\n11. SCAPI returns the enriched response to PWA Kit; the frontend renders cross-linked swatches from `c_relatedSwatches` and constructs PDP navigation URLs client-side from `masterProductID` + `colourValue`.\n\n### 5.2 Component / API Changes\n\n| File / Endpoint | Change Required | Type |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `plugin_zim_scapi/cartridge/scripts/hooks/shop/productModifyGETResponse.js` | Add `buildRelatedSwatches()` helper and a second enrichment block inside `exports.modifyGETResponse`; add `ProductMgr` require | Modified |\n| `hooks.json` (plugin\\_zim\\_scapi) | No change required — `dw.ocapi.shop.product.modifyGETResponse` is already registered | No change |\n| `data/core/meta/system-objecttype-extensions.xml` | Confirm `relatedMasterProductID` attribute (Set of Strings) is declared on the `Product` system object — required if not already deployed | New / Confirm |\n\n### 5.3 SCAPI Hook Specification\n\n**Hook ID:**`dw.ocapi.shop.product.modifyGETResponse`**Script:**`plugin_zim_scapi/cartridge/scripts/hooks/shop/productModifyGETResponse.js`**Exported function:**`exports.modifyGETResponse`\n\n**Input:** Standard SFCC `modifyGETResponse` hook arguments — `product` (dw.catalog.Product), `response` (hook response document)\n\n**New logic added to `productModifyGETResponse.js` (implementation):**\n\nDefaultjavascriptvar ProductMgr = require('dw/catalog/ProductMgr');\nvar swatchLog = Logger.getLogger('zimm.relatedSwatches');\nvar MAX\\_RELATED\\_SWATCHES = 5;\nvar COLOUR\\_ATTR\\_ID = 'color';\nfunction buildRelatedSwatches(masterProduct) {\nvar relatedIDs = masterProduct.custom.relatedMasterProductID;\nif (empty(relatedIDs) || relatedIDs.size() === 0) return null;\nvar swatches = [];\nvar count = 0;\nvar it = relatedIDs.iterator();\nwhile (it.hasNext()) {\nif (count >= MAX\\_RELATED\\_SWATCHES) {\nswatchLog.warn('RelatedSwatch: product {0} has more than {1} related IDs configured — truncated', masterProduct.ID, MAX\\_RELATED\\_SWATCHES);\nbreak;\n}\nvar relatedID = it.next();\nvar relatedProduct = ProductMgr.getProduct(relatedID);\nif (empty(relatedProduct) || !relatedProduct.master) {\nswatchLog.warn('RelatedSwatch: {0} not found or not a master — skipped', relatedID);\ncontinue;\n}\nif (!relatedProduct.online) {\nswatchLog.debug('RelatedSwatch: {0} is not online — skipped', relatedID);\ncontinue;\n}\nvar vm = relatedProduct.variationModel;\nif (empty(vm)) continue;\nvar colourAttr = vm.getProductVariationAttribute(COLOUR\\_ATTR\\_ID);\nif (empty(colourAttr)) continue;\nvar cvIt = vm.getAllValues(colourAttr).iterator();\nwhile (cvIt.hasNext()) {\nvar cv = cvIt.next();\nvar swatchImage = cv.getImage('swatch');\nswatches.push({\nmasterProductID: relatedID,\ncolourValue : cv.value,\ndisplayName : cv.displayValue,\nswatchImageURL : !empty(swatchImage) ? swatchImage.absURL.toString() : null\n});\n}\ncount++;\n}\nreturn swatches;\n}\n// Second enrichment block inside exports.modifyGETResponse, after the badge block:\ntry {\nif (empty(product)) return;\nvar masterProduct = product.isVariant() ? product.getMasterProduct() : product;\nif (empty(masterProduct)) return;\nvar relatedSwatches = buildRelatedSwatches(masterProduct);\nif (relatedSwatches !== null) {\nresponse.c\\_relatedSwatches = relatedSwatches;\n}\n} catch (e) {\nswatchLog.error('modifyGETResponse related swatch enrichment failed for product {0}: {1}', product.ID, e.message);\n}\n\n**Key implementation notes:**\n\n* `product.online` is SFCC's computed property — it already accounts for the online flag, `onlineFrom`, and `onlineTo`. No manual date arithmetic is needed.\n* SFCC Java-style collections use `.size()` (not `.length`) and are iterated with `.iterator()` / `hasNext()` / `next()`.\n* `empty()` is the SFCC runtime global for null/empty checks — used throughout for consistency with the existing hook.\n* `response.c_relatedSwatches` is set as a native JS array — no `JSON.stringify`. The SCAPI response serialises the array directly.\n* The swatch block is in a separate `try/catch` from the badge block — a failure in related swatches does not affect badge enrichment.\n\n**Output — `c_relatedSwatches` response field (appended to SCAPI product response):**\n\nDefaultjson{\n\"id\": \"9536JF261BLK\",\n\"name\": \"Waverly Mini Dress\",\n\"c\\_relatedSwatches\": [\n{\n\"masterProductID\": \"9536JF261CRM\",\n\"colourValue\": \"CRM\",\n\"displayName\": \"Cream\",\n\"swatchImageURL\": \"https://www.zimmermann.com/on/demandware.static/-/Sites-zimmermann-master/default/images/swatch/9536JF261CRM\\_CRM\\_sw.jpg\"\n},\n{\n\"masterProductID\": \"9536JF261NVY\",\n\"colourValue\": \"NVY\",\n\"displayName\": \"Navy\",\n\"swatchImageURL\": \"https://www.zimmermann.com/on/demandware.static/-/Sites-zimmermann-master/default/images/swatch/9536JF261NVY\\_NVY\\_sw.jpg\"\n}\n]\n}\n\n**PWA Kit consumption note:** The frontend reads `product.c_relatedSwatches` from the SCAPI product response as a native array — no `JSON.parse` is required. The PWA Kit constructs the PDP navigation URL client-side using `masterProductID` and `colourValue`. A missing or null `c_relatedSwatches` field means no related swatches are configured — not an error state.\n\n### 5.4 Error Handling & Edge Cases\n\n| Scenario | Expected Behaviour | Type |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Related product ID in `relatedMasterProductID` does not exist in the catalog | Skip with `swatchLog.warn`; do not throw; remaining IDs continue to process | Edge case |\n| Related product exists but is not a master product | Skip with `swatchLog.warn`; do not render a swatch | Edge case |\n| Related product is online but has no `color` variation attribute | Skip silently; `continue` to next ID | Edge case |\n| Swatch image is null for a colour variant | Include swatch entry with `swatchImageURL: null`; frontend renders a fallback (colour name text or placeholder) | Edge case |\n| Product has more than `MAX_RELATED_SWATCHES` (5) related master IDs configured | Process the first 5 IDs only; log a warning with the product ID | Edge case |\n| Hook throws an unhandled exception | Swatch `try/catch` logs the error; badge enrichment is unaffected; PDP must not break | Error |\n| Related product's `online` flag is false, or current date is outside its online date window | `product.online` returns `false`; product excluded from `c_relatedSwatches`; no swatch rendered on PDP | Edge case |\n| `relatedMasterProductID` attribute not yet deployed to the environment | `masterProduct.custom.relatedMasterProductID` will be null/empty; hook exits cleanly with no swatch enrichment | Edge case |\n\n### 5.5 Configuration & Environment Notes\n\n* **Business Manager:** Merchandisers configure `relatedMasterProductID` (Set of Strings) on each master product. The relationship must be set bidirectionally — there is no automatic mirroring.\n* **Catalog XML:** The `relatedMasterProductID` attribute definition must be present in `data/core/meta/system-objecttype-extensions.xml` before hook deployment. Attribute type: `set-of-string`. Per project conventions, the attribute must also be added to an `<attribute-group>` in the same type extension to be visible in Business Manager.\n* **`MAX_RELATED_SWATCHES` constant:** Set to `5` in the initial implementation. Can be promoted to a custom site preference if merchandisers require a higher limit.\n* **All storefronts:** The hook fires for all sites; no per-site configuration is required. `swatchImage.absURL` uses the current request context, so image URLs are site-scoped correctly.\n\n---\n\n6. PWA Kit Frontend Implementation\n----------------------------------\n\n### 6.1 Data Layer\n\n`c_relatedSwatches` is returned automatically in the existing `useProduct` SCAPI call — no additional fetch, no change to the `expand` parameter, and no new hook is required. The product is fetched in the base `product-detail/index.jsx` (not overridden):\n\nDefaulttsxconst { data: productResponse } = useProduct({\nparameters: {\nid: urlParams.get('pid') || productId,\nperPricebook: true,\nexpand: ['availability', 'promotions', 'options', 'images', 'prices', 'variations', ...]\n}\n})\n\n`productResponse.c_relatedSwatches` will be a native array when related colours are configured by a merchandiser, or absent when not configured. SCAPI custom extension fields (`c_*`) are included in the product GET response by default and do not require explicit expansion.\n\nThe `@salesforce/commerce-sdk-react` / `commerce-sdk-isomorphic` SDK types do not declare `c_*` extension fields — a type extension is required (see Section 6.2).\n\n### 6.2 Type Extension\n\nAdd the following to `overrides/app/types/commerce.ts`:\n\nDefaulttsx/\\*\\* One cross-linked colour swatch entry returned by the SCAPI modifyGETResponse hook. \\*/\nexport type RelatedColourSwatch = {\nmasterProductID: string\ncolourValue: string\ndisplayName: string\nswatchImageURL: string | null\n}\n/\\*\\*\n\\* Extends the base SFCC Product type with Zimmermann custom c\\_ extension fields.\n\\* Add new c\\_ fields here as they are introduced via SCAPI hooks.\n\\*/\nexport type ZimmermannProduct<T> = T & {\nc\\_relatedSwatches?: RelatedColourSwatch[]\nc\\_productBadges?: Array<{ productBadge: string; productBadgeUrl: string }>\n}\n\nIn `product-view/index.tsx`, cast the product prop where the `c_relatedSwatches` field is read:\n\nDefaulttsximport type { RelatedColourSwatch, ZimmermannProduct } from 'app/types'\n// Within the component, where the product prop is destructured / accessed:\nconst relatedColourSwatches: RelatedColourSwatch[] =\n(product as ZimmermannProduct<typeof product>).c\\_relatedSwatches ?? []\n\n### 6.3 Component Changes\n\n**File to modify:**`overrides/app/components/product-view/index.tsx`\n\n`Swatch` and `SwatchGroup` are already imported in this file. No new component imports are required.\n\nThe existing colour swatch rendering iterates `variationAttributes` and renders one `SwatchGroup` + `Swatch` per variation value. Cross-linked swatches are appended inside the same `SwatchGroup` for the `color` attribute — they use the same `Swatch` component with `variant=\"circle\"`.\n\n**Changes within the `variationAttributes.map()` block:**\n\nDefaulttsx// After const swatches = values.map(...), before the return:\nconst crossLinkedSwatches = id === 'color'\n? relatedColourSwatches.map(({masterProductID, colourValue, displayName, swatchImageURL}) => {\nconst content = swatchImageURL ? (\n<Box\nheight=\"100%\"\nwidth=\"100%\"\nminWidth=\"32px\"\nbackgroundRepeat=\"no-repeat\"\nbackgroundSize=\"cover\"\nbackgroundColor={displayName.toLowerCase()}\nbackgroundImage={`url(${swatchImageURL})`}\n/>\n) : displayName\nreturn (\n<Swatch\nkey={`cross-${masterProductID}-${colourValue}`}\nhref={crossLinkedSwatchUrl(masterProductID, colourValue)}\nvalue={colourValue}\nname={displayName}\nvariant=\"circle\"\nselected={false}\nisFocusable={false}\n>\n{content}\n</Swatch>\n)\n})\n: []\n// SwatchGroup render — append crossLinkedSwatches after existing swatches:\nreturn (\n<SwatchGroup key={id} value={selectedValue?.value} displayName={selectedValue?.name || ''} ...>\n{swatches}\n{crossLinkedSwatches}\n</SwatchGroup>\n)\n\n**`crossLinkedSwatchUrl` helper (inline in the component file):**\n\nDefaulttsx// Constructs a locale-aware PDP URL for a cross-linked swatch.\n// Replaces the current product ID segment in pathname with the related master ID,\n// preserving any locale prefix (e.g. /en-AU/product/9536JF261BLK → /en-AU/product/9536JF261CRM).\nconst crossLinkedSwatchUrl = (masterProductID: string, colourValue: string): string => {\nconst basePath = location.pathname.replace(/\\/product\\/[^/?]+/, `/product/${masterProductID}`)\nreturn `${basePath}?color=${colourValue}`\n}\n\n`location` is already in scope via `const location = useLocation()` (line 9 of the existing file).\n\n### 6.4 Active Swatch State\n\n| Swatch type | `selected` value | Rationale |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Native colour swatches (current master's variants) | `isSelected` — existing logic `selectedValue?.value === value` | Unchanged. The currently selected colour variant shows as active. |\n| Cross-linked swatches (other masters) | Always `false` | A cross-linked swatch represents a different master product. It is never the \"selected\" colour on the current PDP. When a shopper clicks it, they navigate to the related master's PDP where that product's own native swatches handle the selected state. |\n\nNo changes are required to the existing selected-state logic.\n\n### 6.5 PDP URL Construction\n\nCross-linked swatch `href` pattern: `/{locale}/product/{masterProductID}?color={colourValue}`\n\nThe `crossLinkedSwatchUrl` helper replaces only the product ID segment in `location.pathname`, preserving any locale prefix. This matches the URL shape the existing `buildVariantValueHref` produces for native colour swatches (`/product/{masterID}?color={value}`).\n\nWhen the shopper lands on the related PDP: - `productId` is read from the `:productId` route param (the related master ID) - `useProduct` fetches the related master's product data - `?color=` pre-selects the colour variant via the existing `useVariant` hook - The `useEffect` in `product-detail/index.jsx` subsequently sets `?pid=` to the resolved variant ID\n\nNo routing changes are required.\n\n### 6.6 Files Changed\n\n| File | Change | Tier |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `overrides/app/types/commerce.ts` | Add `RelatedColourSwatch` type; add `ZimmermannProduct<T>` utility type extending SFCC product with `c_*` fields | Tier 3 |\n| `overrides/app/components/product-view/index.tsx` | Read `c_relatedSwatches`; add `crossLinkedSwatchUrl` helper; extend `color` `SwatchGroup` with cross-linked swatch entries | Tier 3 |\n\nNo new files, no routing changes, no new SCAPI fetches, no new package dependencies.\n\n### 6.7 Testing Requirements\n\n| Test type | What to cover | Tool |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Unit (Vitest) | `c_relatedSwatches` entries render as `Swatch` elements with correct `href` containing `masterProductID` and `colourValue`; `selected={false}` on all cross-linked swatches; `swatchImageURL: null` renders `displayName` text fallback; empty `c_relatedSwatches` array renders nothing extra | `overrides/app/components/product-view/index.test.ts` |\n| Unit (Vitest) | `crossLinkedSwatchUrl` produces the correct locale-aware path for a product in a locale-prefixed and a non-prefixed URL | Inline in the same test file |\n| Storybook | Add `WithRelatedColours` story to `product-view` stories showing the extended swatch row with 2 cross-linked entries; add `WithRelatedColoursNoImage` story showing the `swatchImageURL: null` fallback | `overrides/app/components/product-view/index.stories.tsx` |\n| E2E (Playwright) | Covered by the `@p0` scenario in Section 7 — PDP cross-linked swatch click navigates to the correct related PDP pre-selected on the right colour | `e2e/tests/zimm/pdp/` |\n\n### 6.8 Edge Cases (Frontend)\n\n| Scenario | Expected Behaviour |\n| --- | --- |\n| `c_relatedSwatches` is absent or null on the product response | `relatedColourSwatches` defaults to `[]`; `SwatchGroup` renders with existing native swatches only — no visual change |\n| `swatchImageURL` is null for a cross-linked swatch entry | Swatch renders `displayName` text as its child — same fallback pattern as existing native swatches with no image |\n| Cross-linked swatch has the same `colourValue` as a native swatch (e.g. two masters share a colour code) | Both appear in the group; native swatch shows `selected={true}` if currently selected, cross-linked swatch always shows `selected={false}` |\n| Shopper navigates to the cross-linked PDP and back | Full page load both ways; browser back/forward history works normally via React Router |\n\n---\n\n7. Testing & Validation\n-----------------------\n\n### 7.1 Test Coverage\n\n| Test Type | What is Being Tested | Pass Criteria |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Unit (SFCC) | `buildRelatedSwatches()` — online filtering | Products with `online=false` are excluded; online products are included |\n| Unit (SFCC) | `buildRelatedSwatches()` — null product guard | `ProductMgr.getProduct()` returning null does not throw; ID is skipped |\n| Unit (SFCC) | `buildRelatedSwatches()` — non-master guard | Product that is not a master is skipped with a warn log |\n| Unit (SFCC) | `buildRelatedSwatches()` — `MAX_RELATED_SWATCHES` cap | When 6 IDs are configured, only 5 swatch groups are returned and a warning is logged |\n| Unit (SFCC) | `buildRelatedSwatches()` — empty attribute | Null/empty `relatedMasterProductID` returns `null`; `c_relatedSwatches` is not set on response |\n| Unit (PWA) | `product-view` renders cross-linked swatches from `c_relatedSwatches` | Swatch elements with correct `href`, `selected={false}`, and `swatchImageURL: null` fallback |\n| Unit (PWA) | `crossLinkedSwatchUrl` produces locale-aware URL | Correct pathname segment replacement with and without locale prefix |\n| Integration | SCAPI GET `/products/{masterID}` for a product with `relatedMasterProductID` configured | Response includes `c_relatedSwatches` as a native array with correct structure; `c_productBadges` is also present and unaffected |\n| Integration | SCAPI GET for a product with no `relatedMasterProductID` configured | `c_relatedSwatches` is absent; `c_productBadges` is unaffected |\n| E2E / Playwright (@p0) | PDP cross-linked swatch click navigates to correct related PDP pre-selected on the right colour | URL contains correct master ID and colour param; PDP renders the correct product |\n| E2E | PDP for a product with no related colours configured renders without error | No swatch rendering error; existing colour swatches unaffected |\n\n### 7.2 Regression Risk\n\n**SFCC:** The `modifyGETResponse` hook fires on every SCAPI product GET. The swatch enrichment block exits immediately if `relatedMasterProductID` is empty, so the performance impact for products without the attribute is minimal. The badge enrichment block is in a separate `try/catch`, so a swatch failure cannot suppress badge data.\n\n**PWA Kit:**`crossLinkedSwatches` is `[]` when `c_relatedSwatches` is absent — the `SwatchGroup` renders identically to today for products without related colours. The only regression risk is a type cast error if `product` is null when the component renders; this is mitigated by the `?? []` default and the existing null-guards in `product-view`.\n\n---\n\n8. Risks & Mitigations\n----------------------\n\n| Risk | Likelihood | Mitigation | Owner |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Synchronous ProductMgr lookups add latency to product GET for products with many related IDs | Med | `MAX_RELATED_SWATCHES` cap of 5; monitor SCAPI product GET p95 latency in staging after hook deployment | Victor T. Crisostomo |\n| Merchandisers configure the relationship unidirectionally — one PDP shows cross-links, the other does not | High | BM training and documentation; note in the acceptance criteria that QA must verify both directions | Victor T. Crisostomo / Merchandising lead |\n| **OPEN: Image gallery hover behaviour unresolved** — Dani Rivett (product) expects swatch hover in the expanded gallery to swap images without a full-page refresh; the dev team has flagged this requires a different technical approach (prefetching related product images). This is not in scope for this TSD but must be resolved before the frontend team finalises the gallery component. | High | Escalate to Tech Lead and Product for decision before frontend gallery development begins. If in-scope, a separate TSD addendum is required covering the image prefetch contract. | [Technical Lead Name] |\n| `relatedMasterProductID` catalog attribute not deployed to all environments before hook goes live | Med | Confirm attribute deployment in `data/core/meta/system-objecttype-extensions.xml` and attribute group as a deploy pre-condition; hook handles null attribute gracefully | Victor T. Crisostomo |\n| `crossLinkedSwatchUrl` pathname replacement fails on an unexpected URL pattern (e.g. a site without `/product/` in the path) | Low | Validate the regex against all 7 storefront URL patterns in sandbox before merging; add a Vitest test covering locale-prefixed and non-prefixed paths | Victor T. Crisostomo |\n\n---\n\n9. Decision Record\n------------------\n\n| Date | Decision Maker | Decision | Outcome / Rationale |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| 13 Aug 2026 | Dani Rivett, Product | Swatch visibility based on product online flag and online date window — not inventory | Approved AC in SFCC-708 comments. Keeps Coming Soon / Back In Soon products discoverable. |\n| 13 Aug 2026 | Jasmijn Tsang, BA | Image gallery hover (no full-page refresh) is deferred — full-page navigation on swatch click is accepted for this iteration | Technical constraint acknowledged; gallery hover remains an open item for future sprint. |\n| 31 Aug 2026 | Victor T. Crisostomo, Technical Architect | Option A (extend existing `modifyGETResponse` hook) selected over Option B (custom endpoint) | No new hook registration; single network call; server-side filtering; consistent with existing hook and badge pattern (TSD-SFCC-225). |\n| 31 Aug 2026 | Victor T. Crisostomo, Technical Architect | Cross-linked swatches extend the existing `color` `SwatchGroup` in `product-view/index.tsx`; no new component | Minimal change; reuses existing `Swatch`/`SwatchGroup`; avoids a new override file. |\n| [DD MMM YYYY] | [Technical Lead Name] | TSD approved for implementation | Approved — no changes required |\n\n### Sign-off\n\n> ⚠ The TSD is **not approved for implementation** until both rows below are completed.\n\n| Role | Name | Date | Status |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Author | Victor T. Crisostomo | 31 Aug 2026 | Submitted |\n| Technical Lead / Reviewer | [Technical Lead Name] | [DD MMM YYYY] | Pending |",
